<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tenochtitlan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tenochtitlan was the capital city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>, founded in the fourteenth century on an island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>. Connected to the shore by causeways and supported by chinampa agriculture, it grew into one of the largest cities in the world. It was besieged and destroyed by Spanish forces and their indigenous allies in 1521, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> was built on its ruins.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan.jpg" alt="Tenochtitlan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: thomas kole · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_completa_de_Tenochtitl%C3%A1n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
